# Recovered clients and archives (not committed)

`app/mc/` holds the Eaglercraft clients recovered by `tools/recover_clients.py`
(from `archive/all-*.zip`) and `tools/recover_upstream.py` (from the pinned
upstream blobs in `tools/upstream-files.json`). Both are large and are
recovered again after a fresh checkout, so they are git-ignored.

The only tracked file here is `upstream-availability.json`, the manifest the
recovery tool writes once a client directory is complete and verified. The
launcher reads it to enable catalog entries whose files are present.

`archive/` holds the 15-part `all-1.zip` … `all-15.zip` bundle the first
recovery step reassembles. It is likewise git-ignored.
app/mc/*
